## OBLinux: shell theming (THEMING.md item 5) — deliberate, one-time
## exception to the package-list phase's "stock GNOME, no extensions"
## decision. Only the "User Themes" extension from this bundle is
## enabled (see the gschema override); it's an official GNOME-maintained
## extension (part of this upstream package, not third-party), version
## 50.3 verified compatible with the shipped gnome-shell (50.4). Loads a
## CSS file from a stable runtime location — unlike the GDM background's
## gresource-patch approach (item 1), it isn't reverted by every
## gnome-shell update.
gnome-shell-extensions

## OBLinux: networking (replaces releng's iwd/systemd-networkd default;
## NetworkManager is what GNOME Settings' network panel expects)
networkmanager

## OBLinux: AUR support — base-devel/git for building AUR packages generally;
## paru itself comes prebuilt from oblinux_repo (see pacman.conf) rather
## than being built on first login, since it's needed instantly, not a few
## minutes after boot.
base-devel
git

## OBLinux: boot splash (theme: airootfs/usr/share/plymouth/themes/oblinux)
plymouth

## OBLinux: installer + AUR helper + keyboard-layout-preview helper for
## Calamares' keyboard module, from oblinux_repo (not in official repos
## — see pacman.conf's [oblinux_repo] section and docs/CUSTOM_REPO.md for
## how these get built and published). ckbcomp is optional (keyboard
## selection still works without it, just no live preview) but cheap to
## include.
calamares
paru
ckbcomp

## OBLinux: default icon theme (THEMING.md item 4) — amber-accented
## places icons (folders, home icon) on top of papirus-icon-theme,
## from oblinux_repo. See docs/THEMING.md and that repo's own README
## for the full derivation (github.com/marcoobaid/oblinux-icon-theme).
## Set as the default via the gschema override
## (usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/50_oblinux-gdm.gschema.override).
oblinux-icon-theme

## OBLinux: default apps — decided 2026-08-13, see docs/DEFAULT_APPS.md.
## Web browser.
firefox

## Terminal — Ptyxis (modern, GPU-accelerated, actively developed;
## replaces gnome-terminal, which is feature-frozen upstream).
ptyxis

## Core GNOME apps for a functional, appealing out-of-the-box desktop.
gnome-calendar
gnome-calculator
gnome-characters
gnome-clocks
gnome-contacts
gnome-disk-utility
gnome-firmware
gnome-online-accounts
gnome-software
gnome-system-monitor
gnome-text-editor
gnome-weather
baobab
eog
evince
file-roller
fwupd
sushi
totem

## Shell experience — zsh is already the default shell; these give it a
## modern out-of-the-box feel (autosuggestions/syntax-highlighting/prompt)
## without a full framework like oh-my-zsh.
starship
zsh-autosuggestions
zsh-syntax-highlighting

## Modern CLI tools for a "solid terminal" out of the box.
bat
btop
eza
fd
fzf
ripgrep
zoxide

## CLI archive/download tools — gaps in the base list (only
## squashfs-tools was present).
p7zip
unzip
wget
zip

## OBLinux: terminal branding (THEMING.md item 6). fastfetch over
## neofetch — neofetch's upstream maintainer archived that project in
## April 2024; fastfetch is the actively maintained, faster successor
## (confirmed current on Arch: 2.67.1, updated within the same week this
## was added). Config/logo: airootfs/etc/xdg/fastfetch/.
fastfetch

## Codecs — full gst-plugins set (not Fedora's conservative subset), so
## common audio/video formats just work after install.
gst-libav
gst-plugins-bad
gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good
gst-plugins-ugly

## Fonts — base ISO shipped zero desktop fonts before this.
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-liberation

## Fonts — OBLinux defaults (THEMING.md item 3): Inter for desktop UI,
## JetBrains Mono Nerd Font for terminal/monospace (Nerd Font patching
## is what gives starship/eza their icon glyphs). Wired in via
## org.gnome.desktop.interface (see the gschema override) and
## /etc/fonts/local.conf.
inter-font

## NOTE: JetBrains Mono Nerd Font is NOT installed via the
## ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd package (90 files / 228MB for one style used).
## It's vendored directly — see
## airootfs/usr/share/fonts/OBLinux-jetbrains-mono-nerd/ — both to avoid
## that bloat and because this package was the exact, git-bisected trigger
## of a severe live-session boot regression (docs/THEMING.md investigation
## log). Root mechanism unconfirmed; shipping only the 4 files actually
## used removes it as a variable regardless.

## Printing — GNOME Settings' printer panel needs cups running;
## avahi/nss-mdns enable driverless network-printer discovery.
avahi
cups
cups-pdf
nss-mdns

## Bluetooth — GNOME Settings' Bluetooth panel needs the daemon present.
bluez
bluez-utils

## Firewall — ufw over firewalld: simpler mental model, friendlier to
## users switching from macOS/Windows.
gufw
ufw

## Flatpak — portals (xdg-desktop-portal/-gnome, above) were already
## present; gnome-software (above) is the GUI front-end. Flathub remote
## still needs adding as a post-install step, not a package — see
## docs/DEFAULT_APPS.md.
flatpak
